[resource]
script = ExtResource("1")
title = "Navigation Aids"
brief_tooltip = "Spyglass (Z): First-person zoom to scout distant terrain.
Sextant (M): Bird's eye map view of your surroundings.
Requires the item in a unit's inventory."
detailed_text = "[b]Spyglass & Sextant[/b]

[i]Royal Navy officers carried telescopes and sextants as standard equipment. The spyglass let them spot distant landmarks; the sextant, combined with nautical tables, let them fix their position by the stars. On King William Island, these tools were essential for planning any overland journey.[/i]

Two navigation items let you see beyond normal camera range. Both require a unit to have the item in their inventory.

[b]Spyglass (Z)[/b]

Press [b]Z[/b] with a unit selected who has a spyglass. The camera shifts to a first-person view through the telescope.

• The unit must be stopped — you cannot use the spyglass while moving
• Move the mouse to look around (limited to how far a man can turn his head)
• A subtle sway simulates holding the glass by hand
• Press [b]Z[/b] again to exit

Use the spyglass to scout distant terrain, spot landmarks, or check on faraway parts of the island before committing to a journey.

[b]Sextant (M)[/b]

Press [b]M[/b] with a unit selected who has a sextant. The camera rises to a bird's eye view looking straight down.

• Gives you a tactical overview of your camp and surroundings
• Mouse controls are disabled while in this view
• Press [b]M[/b] again to return to normal view

Use the sextant view when planning where to place structures or when you need to see the lay of the land around your position.

[b]Finding These Items[/b]

Spyglasses and sextants can be found in containers salvaged from the ship. Officers often start with one or both. Check unit inventories to see who is carrying what."
screenshot = ExtResource("1_4pf5f")
